# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Versio scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment output from tools/. Every file under here is regenerated by
# Test-RoundTrip.ps1 / Run-Codesys.ps1, and a single visualisation export is
# 2.5 MB - this directory reached 29 MB in one afternoon.
phase0/
scratch/

# Machine-specific state: locks, session ids, logs and pre-import backups.
# A lock committed and pulled onto a colleague's machine is a bug factory.
.versio/local/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CODESYS side files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CODESYS writes these next to any project it opens. They are per-user and per-
# machine, they churn on every open, and they must never be tracked.
#
# The lock marker REPLACES the extension rather than appending to it:
# RefrigeratorControl.project is held by RefrigeratorControl.~u, never by
# RefrigeratorControl.project.~u. The rule here used to be `*.project.~*`, which
# was written from the second, plausible reading and therefore matched nothing at
# all - the marker showed up untracked in every status while three places in the
# code correctly assumed it was ignored. `CodesysProjectFormat.OccupancyMarkerFor`
# and `TransientPatternsFor` have always had it right, and adoption writes the
# scoped form (`plc/Machine.~u`) for repositories it sets up; this repository
# predates that and was typed by hand.
*.opt
*.precompilecache
*~
*.~u
*.autosave
*.bak

# The two directories an export swaps through. Present only mid-export or after a crash.
#
# Staging is where the new tree is built. Trash is the PREVIOUS mirror, moved aside during
# the three-rename swap and deleted once the new one is in place - so a surviving one holds
# a real export and is worth finding rather than committing.
#
# Only staging was listed here, which is the more likely of the two to survive and the less
# alarming to see. Adoption writes both for the repositories it sets up; this repository
# predates that and was typed by hand, which is how one of the pair went missing.
*.versio_staging/
*.versio_trash/
*.codescribe_staging/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pure modules (versio_text, versio_types, versio_yaml, versio_libraries) are
# written to run on CPython as well as on CODESYS's IronPython 2.7, precisely so
# they can be exercised without launching a PLC toolchain. Doing that leaves
# bytecode beside the source, which belongs to whoever ran it and to nothing else.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Downloaded Microsoft bootstrapper, not ours to vendor.
tools/dotnet-install.ps1

# Pack-time downloads and publish output. Pins live in third_party/manifest.json.
# vpk installs under third_party/cache/vpk/ - beside the PortableGit download, and
# out of the source tree, so the covering ignore is the cache one.
artifacts/
third_party/cache/

